  "ref": "JOS.8.24",
  "review_notes": [
    "wherein is read as the three-morpheme fusion of asher with the resumptive bo, whose suffix agrees with the wilderness the clause modifies (rule 22).",
    "they were all fallen: the subject pronoun is the finite verb's (rule 17) and the suffix of kullam is the unrendered occurrence (rule 22), which is how JOS.8.4 reads be ye all ready. The competing reading, giving they to the suffix, is named in that unit's note.",
    "The suffix of tummam keeps its own they, because a suffix on an infinitive construct is that infinitive's subject (rule 18)."
  ]
